  "notes": "sanābhi = 'of the same navel' (kinsman); anyanābhi = of another navel (non-kinsman). pauruṣeya vadha: 'slaying/deadly stroke coming from a man'; 'weapon' is also possible for vadha. 'this one' is left unnamed as in the text.",
  "confidence": "high"
